# docs/PICT_CENSUS.md § S6 — password-set-reuse-gate (#1185)
# lib/auth/server.ts:92 — the shared before-hook enforcing strength + no-reuse-of-last-10 on
# every password-setting auth path. Documented precedence: a wrong current password on
# /change-password takes precedence over the reuse check.
Path:            sign-up, change-password, reset-password, set-password
Strength:        weak, strong
ResetToken:      valid, expired, missing
Session:         present, absent
CurrentPassword: correct, incorrect, missing
Reuse:           reused, not-reused

# ResetToken only means anything on /reset-password (userId resolved from the Verification
# row, not a session) — pin it elsewhere so PICT doesn't waste pairs on a dead parameter.
IF [Path] <> "reset-password" THEN [ResetToken] = "missing";
# Session/CurrentPassword resolve userId on every path except /reset-password (token-based)
# and /sign-up/email (reuse is skipped outright, so userId is never resolved at all).
IF [Path] = "reset-password" THEN [Session] = "absent";
IF [Path] = "sign-up" THEN [Session] = "absent";
# The "wrong current password beats reuse" precedence is /change-password-only.
IF [Path] <> "change-password" THEN [CurrentPassword] = "missing";
